From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eSim Team <esim@fossee.iitb.ac.in>
Date: Sat, 24 May 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ngspice: guard typedef int bool for C23

    Under GCC 15 (default -std=gnu23) `bool` is a reserved keyword,
    so the unconditional `typedef int bool;` in ngspice/bool.h breaks
    the xspice build with:

        error: cannot use keyword 'bool' as enumeration constant
        error: two or more data types in declaration specifiers

    Skip the typedef whenever the compiler advertises C23 (or any
    later C standard) or when the unit is compiled as C++. Pre-C23
    builds keep the legacy behaviour untouched.

    Apply against the ngspice source tree fetched by the eSim Windows
    installer, before invoking `make` in src/xspice/icm.

Signed-off-by: eSim Team <esim@fossee.iitb.ac.in>
---
 src/include/ngspice/bool.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/include/ngspice/bool.h b/src/include/ngspice/bool.h
--- a/src/include/ngspice/bool.h
+++ b/src/include/ngspice/bool.h
@@
+#if !defined(__cplusplus) && \
+    (!defined(__STDC_VERSION__) || __STDC_VERSION__ < 202311L)
 typedef int bool;
+#endif
--
2.50.1
